---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Sketch from '../components/Sketch.astro';
import { base, links } from '../lib';
---
<Base title="About · Defined Once" description="Waylon Sittampalam: analytics engineer in Cary, NC, writing about governed analytics, semantic layers and building with AI.">
  <header class="page-head about-head">
    <div>
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p class="page-dek">I'm Waylon Sittampalam, an analytics engineer in Cary, North Carolina.</p>
    </div>
    <Sketch name="layers" />
  </header>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      I've spent 13 years in analytics — econometrics and forecasting in London, then BI and data modelling in the US.
      Today I'm a senior BI developer working with Power BI, SQL and Snowflake, and moving deeper into governed
      semantic layers and AI-assisted analytics.
    </p>

    <h2>What I care about</h2>
    <p>
      Business users ask the same question and get different answers, because "revenue" is defined five ways across
      five dashboards. Pointing an AI at the raw tables makes it worse. My answer is to define each metric once, in a
      governed layer, and make every answer checkable against it. When something is wrong, I fix the layer, not the
      prompt. That's where the name <em>Defined Once</em> comes from.
    </p>

    <h2>How I work</h2>
    <p>
      I work AI-native: I write the spec, hand AI agents the end-to-end build — exploring data, writing models, tests
      and documentation — and review their output to the same standard as a teammate's. The checks that matter are
      deterministic code, not the model's opinion of itself.
    </p>

    <h2>What I'm building</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href={`${base}/projects/family-learning-tracker/`}>Family Learning Tracker</a> — an AI tutor that marks answers, finds the misconception behind a mistake and targets it the next day.</li>
      <li>Python tooling that checks Power BI semantic models as code: model numbers against source data, and model definitions against naming and query standards.</li>
      <li>A public, end-to-end build of governed natural-language analytics on Snowflake, written up on this blog as it happens.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Background</h2>
    <p>MSc in Finance and Econometrics (Queen Mary University of London) and a BSc in Mathematics (City University).</p>
  </div>

  <div class="post-footer">
    <p class="about-links">
      {links.linkedin && <a href={links.linkedin} rel="me">LinkedIn</a>}
      <a href={`${base}/blog/`}>Read the writing</a>
      <a href={`${base}/rss.xml`}>RSS</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
